x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186097271 1074 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{3-1}f(1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}f(i+1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186100924 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536809 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186100942 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536854 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186100942 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536863 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186100943 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536868 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186100943 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536883 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186105743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536830 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186105756 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536825 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186109303 1078 #edb/ref 17592186109308 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186110776 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536886 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186110778 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536811 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186110778 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536834 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186111263 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535886 17592186045417 true] [17592186111263 1074 "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of t